OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGWOMAN SET FREE AFTER
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGROLLING PIN TRIAL
OL,4,D
OL,5, A woman who killed her husband with a
OL,6, rolling pin over four years ago has
OL,7, been convicted of manslaughter but set
OL,8, free by Luton Crown Court.          F
OL,10,FThe judge said there was no reason to
OL,11,Fimpose a custodial sentence on June
OL,12,FScotland, from Stevenage, Herts, who
OL,13,Fwas sentenced to two years' probation.
OL,15,FThe court heard how Mrs Scotland was
OL,16,Fmentally tortured by her husband,
OL,17,FThomas Scotland, who had also sexually
OL,18,Fabused their daughter.
OL,20,FMr Scotland's body was found last year
OL,21,Fburied in the family's back garden.
OL,23,D]FFromG23-03-92F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
